course: dictionary
lesson: 598
title: Avoid and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word avoid means to keep away from something, or to try not to do something. «Knowing why something is dangerous helps you avoid it even in a new situation.» Here avoid means keep away from danger, even somewhere you have never been before.
explain: Avoid can also mean to stop something happening. «Check your work to avoid mistakes» means check it so that mistakes do not happen. Ask yourself what the sentence wants you to stop, then swap in "try not to" to see if it still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes avoid means to stay away from a person on purpose. Avoid is a verb, so it changes: avoids, avoided, avoiding. The adjective avoidable means something that could be stopped from happening.
fact: To avoid something means to keep away from it.
fact: «Avoid» can also mean to try not to do something, or to stop it happening.
fact: «Avoid» can mean to stay away from a person on purpose.
fact: «Bats are very good at avoiding obstacles» means they can fly around things without bumping into them.
fact: Avoid is a verb: avoid, avoids, avoided, avoiding. Avoidable means something that could be stopped.
exercise: «Knowing why something is dangerous helps you avoid it even in a new situation.» What does avoid mean here? | *Keep away from it | Say hello to it | Make it louder | Go closer to look at it
exercise: «In the UK people value queuing very highly, and jumping the queue makes them upset; knowing such customs helps you avoid offending anyone.» What does avoid offending mean? | *Try not to upset anyone | Go out of your way to upset everyone | Forget your manners | Ask everyone to join in
exercise: Yesterday Sam ___ the puddle on the way to school. | avoiding | *avoided | avoids | avoid
test: «Bats do not get tangled in people's hair; they are very good at avoiding obstacles.» What does avoiding obstacles mean? | *Flying around things so they do not bump into them | Sleeping through the night | Getting stuck in things | Hunting for things to eat
test: Which sentence uses avoid to mean stay away from a person on purpose? | Sam swam across the lake | Sam tidied his room | *Sam avoided his cousin all afternoon after their argument | Sam ate the apple slowly
exam: Which word could replace avoid in «avoid deep water» without changing the meaning? | *Stay away from | Measure | Shout at | Dive into
